  "content": {
    "id": "p27-task56-63-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Find the range of the following functions.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p27-task56-63-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\frac{x^2+4}{2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$R=[2,\\infty)$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2 &\\ge 0\\\\x^2+4 &\\ge 4\\\\\\frac{x^2+4}{2} &\\ge 2\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe minimum is $2$ at $x=0$. Since $x^2$ takes every non-negative value, every output at least $2$ occurs.\n\n$R=[2,\\infty)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-task56-63-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\frac{1}{x}+2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$R=(-\\infty,2)\\cup(2,\\infty)$",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne0$, $\\frac{1}{x}$ takes every non-zero real value.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{x} &\\ne 0\\\\\\frac{1}{x}+2 &\\ne 2\\\\R &=(-\\infty,2)\\cup(2,\\infty)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-task56-63-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\frac{2}{x-1}+3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$R=(-\\infty,3)\\cup(3,\\infty)$",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne1$, $x-1$ takes every non-zero real value. Its reciprocal, and twice its reciprocal, do also.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{x-1} &\\ne 0\\\\\\frac{2}{x-1} &\\ne 0\\\\\\frac{2}{x-1}+3 &\\ne 3\\\\R &=(-\\infty,3)\\cup(3,\\infty)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-task56-63-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\frac{1}{x^2}-5$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p27-task56-63-d-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "R=(-5,\\infty)",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p27-task56-63-d-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\frac{1}{x^2}>0",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " for ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "x\\ne0",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", then subtract ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "5",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "For $x\\ne0$, $x^2$ takes every positive value, so its reciprocal takes every positive value.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2 &>0\\\\\\frac{1}{x^2} &>0\\\\\\frac{1}{x^2}-5 &>-5\\\\R &=(-5,\\infty)\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe lower bound $-5$ is not attained.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-task56-63-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=-\\frac{5}{x^2}+1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p27-task56-63-e-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "R=(-\\infty,1)",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p27-task56-63-e-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Multiplying ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\frac{1}{x^2}>0",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " by ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "-5",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " reverses the inequality; then add ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "1",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "For $x\\ne0$, $\\frac{1}{x^2}$ takes every positive value. Multiplication by $-5$ reverses the inequality.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{x^2} &>0\\\\-\\frac{5}{x^2} &<0\\\\-\\frac{5}{x^2}+1 &<1\\\\R &=(-\\infty,1)\\end{align*}$$\n\nEvery output below $1$ occurs, but $1$ is not attained.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-task56-63-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\sqrt{x+1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$R=[0,\\infty)$",
          "worked": "For $x\\ge-1$, $x+1$ takes every non-negative value, so its square root does also. Zero occurs at $x=-1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sqrt{x+1} &\\ge0\\\\R &=[0,\\infty)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-task56-63-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\sqrt{x}-2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$R=[-2,\\infty)$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\sqrt{x} &\\ge0\\\\\\sqrt{x}-2 &\\ge-2\\\\R &=[-2,\\infty)\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe minimum is $-2$ at $x=0$. Since $\\sqrt{x}$ takes every non-negative value, every output at least $-2$ occurs.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-task56-63-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=4-\\sqrt{x-1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p27-task56-63-h-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "R=(-\\infty,4]",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p27-task56-63-h-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Subtract the non-negative square root from ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "4",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "; equality occurs at ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "x=1",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\sqrt{x-1} &\\ge0\\\\-\\sqrt{x-1} &\\le0\\\\4-\\sqrt{x-1} &\\le4\\\\R &=(-\\infty,4]\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe maximum is $4$ at $x=1$. Since $\\sqrt{x-1}$ takes every non-negative value, subtracting it from $4$ gives every output at most $4$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      }
    ]
